      "description": "Watch Werder Bremen vs RB Leipzig highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 5, 2026. The atmosphere at the Weserstadion was electric on September 5, 2026 , as Werder Bremen hosted RB Leipzig in a highly anticipated Bundesliga clash. Both sides looked to assert their dominance early in a match that promised tactical intrigue and high drama. Early Breakthrough and VAR Intervention Werder Bremen wasted no time igniting the home crowd. Just four minutes into the contest, Eren Dinkci found the back of the net with a clinical right-footed finish following a sharp assist from Chuki . The early goal shifted the momentum, forcing RB Leipzig to search for an immediate response. Despite the visitors controlling much of the ball, the Bremen defense remained disciplined and compact. A major turning point occurred in the 24th minute when the referee initially awarded a penalty to RB Leipzig after Karl Hein was judged to have fouled Christopher Nkunku . However, following a tense VAR review, the decision was overturned. The reprieve gave the hosts a massive boost, allowing them to carry their narrow lead into the halftime break under heavy pressure. Clinical Finishing Seals the Win The second half followed a similar pattern of RB Leipzig possession versus Werder Bremen efficiency. While the visitors finished the game with 71% possession, they lacked the finishing touch displayed by the hosts. In the 68th minute, Niclas Füllkrug doubled the lead with a powerful header from a Marco Grüll cross. Grüll then turned scorer himself in the 80th minute, smashing a right-footed volley into the net to make it 3-0. Leipzig managed a late consolation in stoppage time when Ridle Baku headed home an Andrija Maksimovic cross in the 90+5th minute. However, it was too little, too late for the visitors. In front of 39,700 fans, Werder Bremen secured a statement victory, proving that clinical finishing can triumph over sustained territorial dominance."
